Capture Keyboard Input : Read characters entered by the user from the keyboard.
Handle Backspace : Allow the user to delete the last entered character when Backspace is pressed.
Process Enter Key : Detect the Enter key and treat it as the completion of the user's command.
Manage Input Buffer : Store and manage the characters entered by the user until the command is submitted.
Support Multi character commands : Allow users to enter complete Linux commands containing multiple characters.
Test User Interaction : Test the shell by entering different commands and checking whether keyboard input, backspace, Enter, and command execution work correctly.
